<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malhar Rao Gaekwad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1831–1882</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malhar Rao Gaekwad was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Baroda from 1870 to 1875. In 1874 he was accused of trying to poison the British Resident, Colonel Robert Phayre, with arsenic. A commission of inquiry failed to agree on his guilt, but the British government deposed him in 1875 for misrule, sent him into exile at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> and installed the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayajirao-gaekwad-iii">Sayajirao Gaekwad III</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malhar-rao-gaekwad.jpg" alt="Malhar Rao Gaekwad" width="250" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malhar_Rao_Gaekwad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
